        }
      ],
      "notes": "Scaled for 2 (book makes 2). Score the skin in a 3/4-1 in crosshatch through the fat, salt + rub both sides, dry brine ~3 hr. Book method: two-zone grill, cast-iron pan preheated on the hot side 10 min; skin side down until dark brown, flip and sear 3 min, move breasts to the indirect side to 135°F (~30 min). Sauce in the wiped pan: 2 tbsp butter, shallots till limp, then broth, port, vinegar and cherries reduced by half; mount with 2 tbsp butter. Slice thin on an angle, fan over sauce. No grill at the rental: render skin-side down over medium in cast iron (pour off fat as it builds), flip and sear 3 min, finish in a 300–325°F oven to 135°F; vent the kitchen, it smokes. Save the clean duck fat for potatoes."
    },
